@startuml
' Figure 23.6  The input contract
' Reading order: top to bottom. A Contract names a modality, an owner,
' its fields, and the signals it watches, and has no free-text field.
' The edge admits a RawInput against it and returns an Envelope:
' trust, provenance, fields, signals. Only an Envelope renders into
' context. From inputs.contract and inputs.edge.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
class Contract <<policy>> {
  +name, version: str
  +modality: document | image | voice
  +owner: str
  +fields: Field[]
  +signals: instruction_like, hidden_text
  +free_text = False
}
class Field <<policy>> {
  +pattern: regex
  +accept_at, review_at: float
  +check: pnr | profile | supplier
}
class RawInput <<knowledge>> {
  +channel, sender, received_at
  +layers: visible | hidden
  +extracted: value, conf, where
}
class Envelope <<evidence>> {
  +trust = untrusted
  +provenance: sha256, extractor
  +fields: value, conf, route
  +read_back: amount, date
  +route(): worst field
}
Contract *-down- Field
RawInput .right.> Contract : admitted against
RawInput -down-> Envelope : admit()
Envelope ..> Contract : names version
@enduml
